dbh_plot_late
#there may be a couple of reasons the two lines don't differ in the rotation treatments
#1) suppression in the non-LRR trees also reduced growth (could add suppression flag too, would need to recode)
#Did this and it seemed to help
#2) for the 25y treatments there were so few (if any) trees that had LRR and were alive that they don't mean much (see divergence of CI)
#These charts include only trees that were alive at the time of diameter measurement.  In the "early" phase of the 12y rotations and the "mid" phase of DF, the could have died at a later measurement date (most) or they could have been alive at harvest.
#See if it is possible to add custom ages and diameters at mortality for dead trees? Or is it obvious that trees and died within the measurement window would have reduced growth even if they are alive?
